        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Part V, Line 4: Intended uses of the endowment fund.</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>Elder Laws current spending policy is to disburse 5% of the value of the fund annually, based upon endowment principal market value over the last 36 months. If the market value of the endowment principal of any fund, at the end of each month, is less than the initial value of all contributions made to the endowment principal, then distributions will be limited to interest and dividends received.The endowment funds primarily serve to generate income that may be distributed with Board approval to support programs.</ExplanationTxt>
